when we last caught sight of agent dunn  he was departing new york and making his  way to philadelphia  he had not long since witnessed his  friend being brutally murdered by a  mysterious woman dressed in black  then while on his mission to hunt her  down he discovered the significance of  this woman was much greater than he  could have imagined  and that there is something much bigger  in play  it turned out she'd been working with  rogue division agents the lmb  and has access to a surprisingly large  amount of highly sensitive information  around the shd gathering clues  dunn hopes to uncover what she's up to  and who she's working for  and at this stage all intel is pointing  him towards philadelphia  [Music]  [Music]  heather had always been an exceptional  mediator and had dreams of becoming an  entertainment lawyer  but this all changed when a close friend  was killed during a hostage situation  she knew from then on she wanted to make  a difference in the world  to protect and try to prevent the  senseless loss of innocent lives  so she joined the fbi critical incident  response group where she worked on  providing expertise in crisis management  hostage rescue surveillance crisis  negotiations  behavioral analysis and technical  operations  while pursuing this new line of work she  undertook studies at georgetown  university  where she gained a phd in psychology  it was here that she caught the eye of  the strategic homeland division with  their thesis on the catastrophic mindset  she discussed how catastrophic thinking  can be defined as ruminating about  irrational worst-case outcomes  it can increase anxiety and prevent  people from taking action  in a situation where action is required  and this can be especially true in a  crisis situation  because of this paper she was identified  as an incredibly valuable asset to the  shd  and was recruited into their ranks soon  after  as an optimist and highly skilled in  reading the motivations of others  she is conscious of the overall  well-being of a group of individuals  and is highly empathetic  heather ward was defending a settlement  a settlement that was struggling with  everything  from food and clean water to electricity  and illness  and on top of this constant attacks  they had finally made it through winter  and with spring it brought a new taste  of hope  but although things were looking up they  were still far from fine  while hunting turkey on the outskirts of  their encampment isaac suddenly blipped  alerting her that an unknown agent had  just arrived in philadelphia  turning she saw the figure of a man and  who was pointing her weapon towards her  he shouted out a command for her to show  him her watch  she quickly reciprocates and also calls  out her name and credentials to him  he immediately lowers his gun and  identifies himself as caleb dunn  an shd agent from new york city  he is clearly very defensive and doesn't  seem overly trusting of new people  but she needs him to realize that he's  in her city now and she needs to know  who he is  in order to keep her people safe he  begins describing in detail everything  he had witnessed  from the rogue agents back home to the  newly weaponized lmb  he then asked her about the current  situation in philadelphia  she listens to his information carefully  as she is already well aware of the  current situation in new york  as it was the epicenter of the outbreak  she thinks to herself there must be a  good reason why he would be here  rather than new york as philadelphia is  fearing much better  dunn went on to further explain his  altercations with the mysterious woman  in black  and how he had discovered that  philadelphia is somehow connected  however before they could continue any  further with the conversation they heard  gunfire  and it was coming from the settlement  a local group calling themselves the  founders are attacking hither's  settlement  a collection of tyrannical opportunist  gun nuts they believe that the us was  doomed from the beginning  by the flawed ideals of its founding  fathers they want to rewrite the  constitution  with a form of class-based society and  they to be the masters above everyone  else  they had been attacking the settlement  and its people since february  and while hither and the other agents  had thus far managed to hold them back  it seemed with every failed attack that  they were getting stronger  and somehow better armed  heather and dunn arrive at the scene  without a second thought they engaged  the attacking forces  there used to be a sale of three agents  guarding the settlement but over time  these numbers had dropped it was now  just her  and it had been this way for the last  month  fortunately it didn't take long to scare  off the founders by surprising them  and flanking from behind any founders  still standing after the initial barrage  of bullets  quickly fled the scene  heather explained to dunn about how the  settlement originally started out at the  university hospital  but as the settlement began to quickly  grow it started to attract all sorts of  unsavory folk  so because of this they moved to a  location that was easier to defend  at first the founders were just a  nuisance but then a month ago they  started demanding a weekly tribute for  upholding security  initially heather laughed at them  however when they came back with a  mortar and lmgs  along with a number of other shiny new  toys she started to take notice  it was then that dunn explained that  they are having a similar situation in  new york  where a group thought to be crushed and  disbanded suddenly came back  re-armed and re-militarized with a large  number of new weapons and technology  heather was now beginning to understand  and this was the link that he was  talking about earlier  dunn however wants to be certain so he  inquires of the location of the founders  headquarters  heather introduces dunn to a man named  timmy a former member of the founders  who had abandoned their ranks a month  ago  he left after he witnessed one of the  founder leaders execute his friend  initially heather assumed he was there  to spy on the settlement  so took him in and fed him false intel  but over time he proved himself to be  loyal  and an asset to their cause dunn began  to question him  to find out if he knew of a woman with  short black hair and blue eyes  and who was more than likely an outsider  working alongside the founders  tammy confirmed that he'd seen her and  that she is referred to as  mantis he also shared that everything  started changing after her first visit  however he had no more information to  share with them as he had left not long  after that  heather and dunn asked tommy for his  assistance and showing them how to sneak  inside the founder headquarters  and eventually managed to convince them  to go back and show them the way  closer to the founders compound they  head underground using the sewers so  they can get access to the inner  perimeter  once back above ground isaac alerts them  of a database sample match  mantis is here sneaking through the  compound  isaac once again picks up a familiar  burst transmission  they spot an open door where it seems to  be coming from and advance forward  moving quietly they find the source of  the transmissions  two men are in the room sending out  communications on a radio  with a high risk of bringing all the  founders forces down upon them  dunn decides on stealth and pulls out  his crossbow  firing quickly before the enemy even  knows they're there  he strikes them down one in the head and  the other through the neck  once inside the room they look around  and notice that the place is packed full  of weapons  timmy identifies one of the men as a top  leader among the founders  however mantis is nowhere to be seen  although mantis may not be here they  have still found a huge stash of the  founder's weaponry  so before they head off heather and  timmy rigg the room with explosives  meanwhile dunn bags up the radio  equipment and any documentation he can  find  nevertheless eventually the cover is  blown and a siren starts going off  outside they can hear men shouting and  frantically searching for them  with done taking point they quickly  start making their way out of the room  and towards the exit  barely slowing down to fire at the  guards they make it to the inner  perimeter just as the building explodes  dunn instructs the others to make their  way into the sewers while he remains  behind to cover them  but unfortunately timmy is struck down  in the street  and doesn't make it dunn stops to assist  the fallen man  but he's gone  back in the settlement heather is  distraught that their actions have led  to timmy being killed  she wants to blame dunn for his  obsession of this woman and how it had  been put in this situation  dunn confesses to her the reason why he  needs to catch her so badly  that mantis was responsible for the  death of his friend and fellow agent  heather begins to sense as he speaks  that he has absolutely no intention of  catching this mantis woman alive  she adamantly insists to done that  mantis needs to be interrogated  with all those resources documentation  including the secret defense facilities  within the city and the security systems  she can't possibly be acting alone  dunn contacts faye and tells her of the  sakon transceiver radio that they had  found she suggests that he takes it to  fort meade  as the nsa may have a way of decrypting  it  with the founders now out of the picture  heather's protection is no longer  necessary for the settlement  she's ready to get out there and help  others so she insists that she's coming  along with dunn for the journey  plus it'll mean that she's there to  ensure that he doesn't just kill mantis  outright  as soon as he catches sight of her  i'm quite enjoying the comic strips that  have been used in the background to  assist in building the scene when  telling the story  i feel it adds a bit more where some  gameplay just really doesn't cut it  maybe i need to find an artist to help  me out again if you weren't aware this  has been part two  of the division comic book series that  came out at the beginning of the  division two  you can find these on darkhorse.com  anyway thank you very much for watching  and i'll catch in the next one  cheers  [Applause]  [Music]  hmm

